{
  "id": "u10-l07",
  "unit": "u10-culture",
  "title": "With close friends",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**তুই** is the language of real closeness: best friends, siblings, cousins your age. Among Bangladeshi friends you'll hear **দোস্ত** ('buddy') constantly. Used with a stranger or an elder, তুই is an insult — so only *answer* in তুই once someone uses it with you.\n\n'Let's…' = **চল / চলো / চলেন** + the আমি-form of the verb:\n\n- **চল, মেলায় যাই** (tui) — 'Let's go to the fair'\n- **চলো, যাই** (tumi) — 'Let's go'\n- **চলেন, চা খাই** (apni) — 'Shall we have tea?'\n\nতুই futures end in **-বি**: **আসবি?** 'Will you come?', **কী খাবি?** 'What'll you have?'",
